9. Pizzo FX / Options Dealer-Positioning Research
The Pizzo FX research thread explored options-market concepts such as dealer positioning, implied volatility, strikes, expiries, gamma-like behavior and liquidity. The project direction was to investigate these mechanisms statistically rather than treating practitioner explanations as established facts.
Large option strikes may become relevant liquidity/attention zones.
Dealer hedging behavior can differ depending on positioning and volatility regime.
Estimated gamma exposure can potentially help classify whether price is more likely to experience pinning/mean-reversion-like behavior or stronger movement.
Implied volatility and skew can provide information about expected risk and asymmetry.
Options positioning should generally be a context layer rather than a tick-level entry trigger unless high-quality data are available.
News can overwhelm positioning effects by changing volatility expectations and macro pricing.
Missing options data should produce an explicit lower-confidence state rather than fabricated estimates.
10. Mukasa Reef / Practitioner Order-Flow Concepts
The discussions also asked to incorporate order-flow strategies described in Mukasa Reef educational videos. The agreed methodological approach is to treat these ideas as practitioner hypotheses and translate them into measurable rules before combining them with the broader system.
Define the exact event described by the practitioner.
Specify its lookback window.
Define threshold and normalization.
Define the required market location.
Define confirmation and invalidation.
Measure whether it adds incremental predictive value after VWAP/value, structure and delta are already present.
Reject concepts whose apparent advantage disappears out of sample.
11. News Intelligence and Interaction With the Strategy
News was discussed as an active market-state variable rather than merely a calendar filter. The EA should distinguish the period before an event, the immediate reaction, confirmation and the subsequent stabilization.
News phase
Potential market behavior
System response
Pre-news
Compression, reduced liquidity, positioning
Reduce risk or block new entries.
Immediate release
Spread/volatility spike, discontinuous repricing
Usually wait; specialized news mode only if proven.
Initial reaction
Directional impulse may be challenged
Do not assume first move is final.
Confirmation
Market begins accepting a direction/level
Reclassify regime; continuation may become preferred.
Post-news stabilization
Volatility normalizes or second move develops
Return to normal strategy rules when execution quality recovers.

11.1 News modes in V36.1
NEWS_OFF — news ignored.
NEWS_FILTER_ONLY — news affects whether trading is permitted.
NEWS_TRADE — news reactions can create trades.
NEWS_HYBRID — news modifies the normal strategy/regime engine.
Historical news features discussed included surprise, reaction requirements and a 30-minute news buffer. V36.1 recorded InpMinSurprisePct = 0.05, InpNewsBufferMins = 30 and InpRequireReaction = true.
