12.2 Exit concepts discussed
ATR-based initial stops.
Structural invalidation rather than arbitrary stop placement.
Partial profit around approximately 2R was part of the V36-era configuration.
Trailing stop using an ATR multiplier, with 1.5× ATR discussed.
Mean-reversion targets around VWAP, POC or value.
Continuation targets around liquidity pools and structural objectives.
Exit when the original hypothesis is invalidated.
Use MAE/MFE and time-to-target analysis to determine whether exit rules actually add expectancy.
