25. Target Final Decision Pipeline
DATA → DATA QUALITY → MARKET STATE → LOCATION → HYPOTHESIS SELECTION → SETUP → ORDER-FLOW CONFIRMATION → NEWS/OPTIONS CONTEXT → ML GATE → RISK GATE → EXECUTION → MANAGEMENT → ATTRIBUTION
The architecture should behave as a hierarchy. Hard safety constraints always outrank probabilistic signals. A high model score cannot override an abnormal spread, invalid data, a daily loss limit, an imminent prohibited news event or a broker-compatibility failure.
26. Standard for Proving the Strategy
Convert every practitioner idea into a measurable hypothesis.
State the expected mechanism.
Specify the observable variables.
Find academic/statistical evidence where available.
Test against a simple baseline.
Test incremental value after controlling for other features.
Evaluate out of sample.
Include costs and execution.
Test across instruments and regimes.
Report uncertainty and robustness, not only profitability.
27. Consolidated Project Status
The project has converged on two major strategy hypotheses: mean reversion/value reversion and trend/continuation.
The adaptive regime selector is the main conceptual bridge between these strategies.
VWAP, volume profile/value area and order flow are intended to interact as contextual evidence.
Pizzo FX/dealer-positioning concepts are positioned as higher-level context requiring rigorous validation.
Mukasa Reef/practitioner order-flow concepts are treated as hypotheses to formalize and test.
News is treated as a dynamic market-state variable.
The ML layer is best positioned as a gatekeeper/probability estimator after the rule-based baseline is reliable.
MQL5 remains the execution and hard-risk authority.
Python can handle heavier research, feature engineering and model services.
Causal feature construction and elimination of look-ahead bias are prerequisites to trusting performance results.
Broker-specific symbol normalization is essential, demonstrated by the XAUUSDm spread-gate problem.
The next major milestone is a causally correct, broker-normalized, walk-forward-tested regime engine that can choose between MR and continuation.
